{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensing (obstacle events) from motion commands. The specification encodes a conservative exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states for coverage, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger recovery turns. Recovery states enable only one turn direction or full_rotate as required, and return to exploration as soon as the path is clear. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state, and only one controllable is enabled per state to avoid oscillations.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion, with all events explicitly modeled.",
